  "Question": "Let \\[ \\begin{aligned} T={}&\\frac1{3-\\sqrt8} -\\frac1{\\sqrt8-\\sqrt7}\\\\ &+\\frac1{\\sqrt7-\\sqrt6} -\\frac1{\\sqrt6-\\sqrt5}\\\\ &+\\frac1{\\sqrt5-2}; \\end{aligned} \\] then",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(T\\lt1\\)",
    "B": "\\(T=1\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\lt T\\lt2\\)",
    "D": "\\(T\\gt2\\)",
    "E": "\\(\\displaystyle\nT=\\frac1{\\substack{(3-\\sqrt8)(\\sqrt8-\\sqrt7)(\\sqrt7-\\sqrt6)\\\\\n{}\\cdot(\\sqrt6-\\sqrt5)(\\sqrt5-2)}}\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "D",
  "Solution": "Each denominator is the difference of square roots of consecutive integers. Multiplying by the corresponding sum makes the denominator equal to \\(1\\). For \\(k=5,6,7,8,9\\), the denominator is positive, and\n\\[\n\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{k}-\\sqrt{k-1}}\n=\\frac{\\sqrt{k}+\\sqrt{k-1}}{k-(k-1)}\n=\\sqrt{k}+\\sqrt{k-1}.\n\\]\nApplying this identity gives\n\\[\n\\begin{aligned}\nT={}&(3+\\sqrt8)-(\\sqrt8+\\sqrt7)\\\\\n&+(\\sqrt7+\\sqrt6)-(\\sqrt6+\\sqrt5)\\\\\n&+(\\sqrt5+2).\n\\end{aligned}\n\\]\nEvery interior radical appears once with each sign, so \\(T=3+2=5\\). Thus \\(T>2\\), and the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
